          "entities": {},
          "text": "A Star is Born — with Jet Engines!\n\nThis stunning image shows Herbig-Haro object HH111, a dramatic result of a newborn star blasting out high-speed jets of ionized gas.\n\nThese plasma jets collide with nearby clouds at hundreds of kilometers per second, lighting them up and forming structures like HH111. This one stretches 2.6 light-years and is powered by a young star buried in a dense cloud about 1,300–1,500 light-years away in Orion.\n\nThe image was taken in infrared by Hubble’s Wide Field Camera 3, allowing us to see through the dust and reveal what’s usually hidden.\n\nCredit: ESA/Hubble & NASA, B. Nisini"
        },
